# MANIFEST: what editing bay 1 carries of its own home, for `../sync`.
#
# Everything here is hand-built and in no other repository: the `~/code` root
# this bay's sessions start in, its tools, and its list of mirrors. Losing the
# disk loses all of it, so it is carried as text with history, where a person
# or an agent can read the diff before it is put back (station-node's
# `machine/CARRYING.md`: this restores what someone decided should be there,
# not what was there).
#
#   mode    repo path (relative to this folder)   home path (relative to ~)
#
# mirror    the repository holds a copy. `sync install` puts it in place,
#           `sync mirror` brings the machine's copy back for a pull request,
#           and `sync status` says which side differs. A copy, not a link: this
#           bay keeps no live checkout for a link to point into, and a link
#           into refs/ would make the read-only mirror the thing being edited.
# clone     a list of repository URLs, one per line; `sync install` clones any
#           that are missing into the home directory named, and never touches
#           one that is there.
#
# NOT HERE, AND WHY:
# - fcpublicmedia.org itself. It is how these bytes arrive, so it is cloned
#   by hand on Day 0 (PROFILE.md).
# - station-node's mirror. It is read here, and it is somebody's own
#   repository; it is cloned by hand, and not named in a public file.
# - Session state, memory and the pool's snapshot. They are in
#   %LOCALAPPDATA%\editing-bay-1 and ~/.claude, and none of it is a decision.

mirror  code/AGENTS.md         code/AGENTS.md
mirror  code/CLAUDE.md         code/CLAUDE.md
mirror  code/bin/refs          code/bin/refs
mirror  code/bin/pool.ps1      code/bin/pool.ps1
mirror  code/refs.wanted       code/refs.wanted

clone   code/refs.wanted       code/refs

# Machine-global git ignores: `.pr` stays out of every repository here.
mirror  home/git/ignore        .config/git/ignore

# The crew's one switch (../fcpm), by name in any window: the shim, and its
# folder on this user's PATH. After the first `fcpm install`, a person or a
# session types `fcpm`, never a path or an interpreter.
mirror    home/bin/fcpm.cmd      .local/bin/fcpm.cmd
path      -                      .local/bin

# What sessions here may run without asking: this profile's GRANTS, compiled.
# Placed by `fcpm install`, which a person runs; never by a session.
settings  editing-bay-1          code/.claude/settings.json
